  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nHigh pressure is slowly sliding west over the great basin region \nwill become the main weather headliner for the next week and and \nhalf, but models hint at a parting shot of mid level moisture \nMonday afternoon. With the majority of the region staying dry and \nvery warm, for UT/NV border area, convective buildups will be \nlikely across eastern NV and even a low 20% to 20% chance for a \nisolated thunderstorm or two will be possible. The best chances \nwill be along the UT/NV border and could reach Ely and West \nWendover. However any precipitation that reaches the ground will \nbe brief and very light as storm motion limits accumulations. \nTuesday through next Monday mid/long range models are resolute in \nthe return of quiet Summertime conditions, with breezy afternoon W\nto SW winds, and very warm temperatures. as the upper ridge \nbuilds in over the southern Great Basin. Fire weather, and Heat \nRisk conditions will need to be watched closely as the drying out \nof both the land and atmosphere commences, and heat builds, \novernight relief will be brief if any. Winds will be out of the \nwest to SW with breezy afternoon winds ranging at 10 to 20 MPH \nwith gusts up to 30 MPH possible. Temperatures will range in the \nmid 90s to mid 100s. A heat advisory in effect for sections of \nElko County for Sunday, and may need to be expanded as heat \nimpacts build through the week. As for Fire weather, RH percent \nvalues will drop into the low teens to single digits in the \nafternoons, with overnight recoveries only making it back to the \nupper 20s, combined with afternoon winds may lead to periods of \nelevated to critical fire weather conditions. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is moderate confidence for a low chance of a few isolated \nthunderstorms Monday afternoon for far eastern NV. \n\nThere High confidence in the return of quiet Summertime \nconditions, with breezy afternoon winds and very warm temperatures\nTuesday through the start of next week.",
